eeds to build momentum, and the landlord only has 7 cards (a critical advantage), I should take control here with ♥2 rather than let the landlord lead again.\n\nReason:\n\nI\'ll play ♥2. The landlord has only 7 cards remaining and poses an immediate threat. If I pass, the landlord regains control and can lead with any combination, potentially playing out quickly. Using ♥2 (rather than the more valuable BlackJoker) allows me to take control and prevent the landlord from dictating play. This gives me the lead to potentially start breaking down my hand strategically.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥2"]}'}
